From 772524f7943762dd9344960580020e70479a771c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sammyz <2353166+sammyz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:17:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vold: verify mona synthetic-password credentials through
 AIDL Gatekeeper

The old HIDL getService call fails before PIN verification on stock mona,
whose Gatekeeper HAL exposes AIDL. Add a property-scoped verification-only
client and submit the resulting HardwareAuthToken to Keystore. Fail closed
on service/credential/token errors, honor timeout failures, and do not enroll
or replace existing credentials. Keep legacy HIDL behavior for other builds.

Import unchanged AOSP Gatekeeper V1 interface snapshots with their original
licenses and provenance. Adapt their build to this recovery's existing
wire-compatible KeyMint V1 HardwareAuthToken. Include client objects in
static libvold for legacy Make consumers.

Verified PIN unlock, twrp.user.0.decrypt=1, readable internal Android storage,
and concurrent System and DE Data file reads on XT2517-1 Android 15.

Codex was used to make the new integration and testing changes at sammyz's
direction. Imported AOSP interface definitions remain credited to AOSP.

