+# Recovery Gatekeeper AIDL client interface
+
+The three AIDL source files and their V1 API snapshots are unchanged AOSP
+Gatekeeper V1 files from:
+https://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/refs/heads/android15-release/gatekeeper/aidl/aidl_api/android.hardware.gatekeeper/1/
+
+Original AOSP copyright and Apache-2.0 notices are retained. The Android.bp
+integration is a Codex adaptation for this pinned Android 12.1 recovery only.
+It imports KeyMint V1, whose HardwareAuthToken parcel fields match KeyMint V3
+on the tested mona firmware. The generated Gatekeeper client is linked into
+libvold statically so legacy Make consumers receive its code; those consumers
+also link the existing KeyMint V1 parcelable library explicitly.
+
+The client uses the stock android.hardware.gatekeeper.IGatekeeper/default
+service. It only verifies the existing synthetic-password credential and
+forwards the HAL's HardwareAuthToken to Keystore authorization. It does not
+enroll, reset, delete, or re-enroll credentials, including on STATUS_REENROLL.
+It fails on rejected credentials, timeouts, unavailable services, or token
+submission failures. PINs and derived password tokens are not logged.
+
+Codex was used to implement, build, and test the integration at sammyz's
+direction. The interface definitions remain AOSP's work. Verified on XT2517-1
+V2VAS35.29-49-1: PIN accepted, user 0 CE storage unlocked, System and Data file
+reads successful together. Recovery-only opt-in: ro.mona.gatekeeper_aidl=true.
